Added a `Strict Objects` option to the IP Fabric job, naming the object types whose reported value is checked rather than taken on trust. It applies on top of the sync scope, to the types a run already covers: for a supporting object the check is that the name IP Fabric reported resolves to something Nautobot already holds, so that a typo is reported instead of minting a near duplicate; for an IP Address it is that a usable subnet was reported for it; for an Interface it is that IP Fabric reported the Interface, so no placeholder is invented to hold a management address reached through NAT. Locations, Manufacturers, Device Types, Roles, Platforms, Statuses, Virtual Chassis, Interfaces and IP Addresses can each be selected, and each default can be set for the whole instance with an `ipfabric_strict_<type>` setting. Only IP Addresses is selected by default; every other type keeps today's behaviour of filling the gap itself.
